  <title>Manufacturing history</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>Reports</gui><gui>Products</gui><gui>Manufacturing
  history</gui></guiseq> looks back over <link
  xref="manufacturing">manufacturing projects</link>, with the time punched
  on each in the time clock.</p>

  <terms>
    <item><title><gui>Jobs</gui></title>
    <p>Every project, with its quantity, the time it took in total and per
    piece, and the employees who worked on it. Type into <gui>Name</gui> or
    <gui>Product</gui> to narrow the list. Double click a project to see its
    batch notes, and its serial numbers with the customer each was sold
    to.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Summary</gui></title>
    <p>Each product made, with the total pieces and time, and the average,
    shortest and longest time per piece.</p>
    <p>Choose a price level in <gui>Use price level</gui> to compare each
    finished product's minutes per piece with its profit, the price at that
    level less its cost. <gui>Chart</gui> draws the comparison.</p></item>
  </terms>

  <p>Each tab has its own <gui>Refresh</gui> and <gui>Export hub</gui>; see
  <link xref="report_hub"/>.</p>

</page>
